# Defect 508 and panel 199's R2, ratified 2026-10-09: the sitting's `mixed`,
# `climbs(helper(n))`, ran at `-O2` until `timeout` stopped it (exit 124),
# the self-call in tail position turned into a jump. Panel 199's R1 refuses
# `mixed` itself now (`tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-457-*`, `helped`), since
# its helper only computes; this one's helper may end the program, on a path
# no run takes, so `check` lets the function through (reading R4) and the
# run is the witness: the `-O2` words keep a call a call
# (`-fno-optimize-sibling-calls`), and it aborts at every level. Which frame
# ran out is named where the platform names one, and is not asked here.
# Under the sanitiser the runtime's guard yields to ASan, which says
# `stack-overflow`. clang's *all paths through this function will call
# itself* was TRUE here, and is not passed on since panel 199's R3
# (`-Wno-infinite-recursion`): what R4 lets through is where clang's warning
# cannot tell true from false, the call that may end the program coming
# before the self-call, so the run is this shape's witness and lands with R3.
function helper(n: i64) -> i64
    if n < 0
        exit(code: 1)
    return n + 1

function climbs(n: i64) -> i64
    return climbs(helper(n))

function main()
    print(climbs(1))
